course: dictionary
lesson: 1779
title: Weather and climate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Weather is what the sky does today: rain, sun, wind or fog. Climate is the usual weather of a place over many years, about 30 years or more. Climate is the pattern, and weather is one day.
explain: «The sea warms up and cools down slowly, so it makes the climate of coasts milder.» Milder means not so hot and not so cold. The clue is the slow warming and cooling of the sea, which keeps the air around the coast gentler.
explain: «Climate change harms both people and nature, including people far away and people in the future.» Harms means hurts. Climate change is the Earth's climate slowly changing, mostly getting warmer. Climate can also mean the general mood of a group, as in a friendly climate in class, so always check the clues around it.
fact: Climate means the usual weather of a place over many years.
fact: Weather is what happens today; climate is the pattern over about 30 years.
fact: Climate zones include tropical, desert, temperate and polar.
fact: Climate change means the Earth's climate is slowly changing, mostly getting warmer.
fact: «Burning coal, oil and gas» puts gases into the air that warm the climate of the whole planet.
exercise: «The sea warms up and cools down slowly, so it makes the climate of coasts milder.» What is the climate of a place? | How many people live there | What the sky is doing on one day | The name of its biggest river | *Its usual weather over many years
exercise: Which word describes what the sky is doing today? | *Weather | Mood | Climate zone | Climate
exercise: Mrs Hart says the class has a friendly climate. What does climate mean here? | Usual rainfall | Hot and dry | *The general mood of a group | A gas in the air
test: «Climate change harms both people and nature.» What does harms mean? | *Hurts | Helps | Measures | Paints
test: Which of these is a climate zone? | *Polar | Smoke | Weather | Mood
exam: «Burning coal, oil and gas also puts smoke and carbon dioxide into the air, which warms the climate of the whole planet.» What does this sentence say warms the planet's climate? | *Burning coal, oil and gas | Cows burping in the fields | Sea water cooling down | Rain falling on the hills
